  "query_preview": "../Wednesday through Friday/...\n\nConfidence in the long term forecast is fairly high, in that there \nis great agreement on a large high being situated over the Gulf of \nAlaska through almost the end of the workweek. This will lead to \nmostly light winds, with the exception of Wednesday. As a low \nrecedes south of Haida Gwaii further towards British Columbia and a \ntongue of high pressure comes back south to the Gulf from south-\ncentral Alaska, gradient driven winds will be stronger, but weaken \nover time into Thursday for the upper inner channels, such as Lynn \nCanal and Stephens Passage.\n\nThe next pattern change will come with the end of the work week, as \na front moves toward the area later Friday into Saturday as the\nhigh breaks down. Guidance has slowed the onset of impacts with \nthis latter system from run-to-run. At this length of forecast, \nconjecturing at exact impacts is a fool's errand, but elevated \nwinds for most of the panhandle, as well as the next bout of \nnotable rainfall are expected. An early estimate of rain onset \nwould be Friday PM for the northern panhandle",
